# Concurrency suite

The file you are editing takes part in running several Access instances at once:
one gate lane per database, instance creation and ownership, dialogs, screenshots,
or callbacks. Unit tests mock COM, so they cannot catch two real instances
colliding.

Before you finish, run the opt-in suite in the venv. It is skipped by every other
run, including `-m integration`:

```powershell
pytest tests/test_concurrency_integration.py --run-concurrency -v
```

It opens up to three visible Access windows for a few minutes and closes only the
ones it started. In `tools.py`, it is needed only for changes to the `vcs_tool`
wrapper, `_lane_target`, or a tool's gate or instance handling, not for wording or
result fields. If you cannot run it, say so in your summary.
